          "text": "The peak positions index well as a monoclinic ordered-vacancy derivative of the NdSb rocksalt structure. The strongest diagnostic reflections are approximately:\n\n- 7.37\u00b0: 002\n- 13.63\u00b0: 010\n- 14.13\u00b0: 100\n- 14.78\u00b0: 004 + 10\u22122\n- 17.02\u00b0: 102\n- 19.68\u00b0: 110\n- 22.25\u00b0: 006/104\n- 27.45\u00b0: 020\n- 28.48\u00b0: 200\n- 29.81\u00b0: 008\n\nThese give monoclinic \\(P2/c\\), \\(Z=4\\), with \\(a\\approx6.354\\), \\(b\\approx6.491\\), \\(c\\approx24.330\\) \u00c5 and \\(\\beta\\approx99.63^\\circ\\). The long axis and \\(h0l:l=2n\\) condition account for the first peak being 002 rather than 001.\n\n### Primary CIF\n\n```cif\ndata_Nd4Sb3\n_audit_creation_method\n'Indexed from the supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern; ordered-vacancy starting model'\n\n_chemical_name_common                  'neodymium antimonide Nd4Sb3'\n_chemical_formula_structural           'Nd4Sb3'\n_chemical_formula_sum                  'Nd4 Sb3'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                  4\n\n_symmetry_cell_setting                 monoclinic\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M         'P 1 2/c 1'\n_symmetry_Int_Tables_number            13\n_space_group_crystal_system            monoclinic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt              'P 1 2/c 1'\n_space_group_IT_number                 13\n\n_cell_length_a                         6.354\n_cell_length_b                         6.491\n_cell_length_c                         24.330\n_cell_angle_alpha                      90\n_cell_angle_beta                       99.63\n_cell_angle_gamma                      90\n_cell_volume                           989.3\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type                 'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength           1.5406\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn          6.32\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-x,y,-z+1/2'\n3  '-x,-y,-z'\n4  'x,-y,z+1/2'\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nNd  0\nSb  0\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nNd1 Nd 4 g  0.0200  0.0200  0.0100  1.0  1.0\nNd2 Nd 4 g  0.4800  0.4800  0.0100  1.0  1.0\nNd3 Nd 4 g  0.4800  0.0200  0.1250  1.0  1.0\nNd4 Nd 4 g  0.0200  0.4800  0.1250  1.0  1.0\nSb1 Sb 4 g  0.4900  0.0200  0.0050  1.0  1.0\nSb2 Sb 4 g  0.0100  0.4800  0.0050  1.0  1.0\nSb3 Sb 4 g  0.0100  0.0200  0.1250  1.0  1.0\n```\n\nThe lattice and \\(P2/c\\) extinction assignment are considerably better constrained than the individual coordinates. The coordinates above describe the surviving ordered-Sb-vacancy topology and are suitable as a Rietveld/direct-space starting model; precise positional parameters and displacement factors would require full profile refinement against the supplied pattern.",
